---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "FR4GZ: What Frag Means, Frag Movies and FPS History"
description: "What frag means in gaming, plus classic frag movies, famous esports plays, an FPS slang glossary and the history of fragging from Doom to Valorant."
faqs:
  - q: "What does frag mean in gaming?"
    a: "A frag is a kill in a multiplayer game, usually a first-person shooter. To frag someone is to kill them. Games such as Doom and Quake counted frags on the scoreboard, and the word spread from there to almost every shooter."
  - q: "Where does the word frag come from?"
    a: "It comes from military slang. A frag is a fragmentation grenade, and during the Vietnam War fragging meant deliberately attacking a fellow soldier, often an officer, with one. Gamers borrowed the word in the 1990s and gave it a much lighter meaning."
  - q: "What is a frag movie?"
    a: "A frag movie is an edited video of a player's best kills, usually set to music. They started in the Quake and Counter-Strike communities, where players recorded demo files of their games and cut the highlights together."
  - q: "Why is it spelt fr4gz?"
    a: "Fr4gz is frags written in leetspeak, the style of swapping letters for numbers and symbols that grew out of hacker and bulletin board culture and was common in early online gaming. The 4 stands for an A, and the z replaces the plural s."
  - q: "Are the videos hosted on this site?"
    a: "No. Every video is embedded from YouTube and belongs to its creator. Videos only load from YouTube when you press play, using YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode."
---
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}
{%- set featured = (videos | selectattr("featured") | first) %}
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap hero__inner">
    <div class="hero__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ icon("crosshair") }} Player one has entered the arena</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title" data-text="FR4GZ">FR<span>4</span>GZ</h1>
      <p class="hero__def"><span class="mono">frag</span> <span class="hero__ipa">/fræɡ/</span> <em>noun, verb</em>: a kill in a multiplayer shooter. To frag someone is to take them out.</p>
      <p class="lede">Classic frag movies, the plays esports crowds still talk about, the slang you hear in voice chat, and how a grim bit of military slang became gaming's favourite word.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#videos">{{ icon("play") }} Watch frag movies</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/glossary/">{{ icon("book") }} Learn the slang</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="killfeed" aria-hidden="true">
      <p class="killfeed__head">Kill feed</p>
      <ol>
        <li><b class="k-g">Thresh</b> <i>rocket</i> <b>Entropy</b></li>
        <li><b class="k-g">coldzera</b> <i>awp</i> <b>Liquid</b></li>
        <li><b class="k-g">s1mple</b> <i>noscope</i> <b>Fnatic</b></li>
        <li><b class="k-g">Cooller</b> <i>railgun</i> <b>you</b></li>
        <li><b class="k-g">you</b> <i>headshot</i> <b>boredom</b></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="killfeed__score"><span>FRAGS <b>{{ videos.length }}</b></span><span>K/D <b>&infin;</b></span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- if featured %}
<section class="featured" aria-labelledby="featured-heading">
  <div class="wrap featured__inner">
    <div class="featured__player">
      <a class="vid__player vid__player--large" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v={{ featured.id }}" data-yt="{{ featured.id }}" data-title="{{ featured.title }}" aria-label="Play video: {{ featured.title }}">
        <img src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/{{ featured.id }}/hqdefault.jpg" alt="" width="480" height="360" decoding="async">
        <span class="vid__play">{{ icon("play") }}</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="featured__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Featured frag movie</p>
      <h2 id="featured-heading">{{ featured.title }}</h2>
      <p class="vid__channel">{{ featured.game }} &middot; {{ featured.channel }}</p>
      <p>{{ featured.blurb }}</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/videos/">See all {{ videos.length }} videos {{ icon("arrow") }}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}

<section class="define" id="what-is-a-frag" aria-labelledby="define-heading">
  <div class="wrap define__inner">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Dictionary</p>
      <h2 id="define-heading">What is a frag?</h2>
      <p>In gaming, a <strong>frag</strong> is a kill, usually in a first-person shooter. Doom and Quake counted frags in deathmatch, so the word stuck, and players still say they fragged someone, went on a fragging spree or watched a frag movie.</p>
      <p>The word is older and darker than games. It comes from the <strong>fragmentation grenade</strong>, and in US military slang from the Vietnam War, fragging meant deliberately attacking a fellow soldier, often a superior officer, with one. Gamers borrowed the word in the 1990s and turned it into something far less serious.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/history-of-fragging/">Read the history of fragging {{ icon("arrow") }}</a>
    </div>
    <dl class="dict">
      <div class="dict__entry">
        <dt><span class="mono">frag</span> <em>noun</em></dt>
        <dd><ol><li>A kill in a multiplayer video game.</li><li>A fragmentation grenade.</li></ol></dd>
      </div>
      <div class="dict__entry">
        <dt><span class="mono">frag</span> <em>verb</em></dt>
        <dd><ol><li>To kill another player in a game. <q>She fragged the whole squad.</q></li><li>US military slang: to deliberately kill or wound a fellow soldier or superior officer with an explosive device.</li></ol></dd>
      </div>
      <div class="dict__entry">
        <dt><span class="mono">fr4gz</span> <em>leetspeak</em></dt>
        <dd>Frags, written the way it would have appeared in a 1990s clan name or IRC channel.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap listing" id="videos">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Frag movies and famous plays</h2>
    <a class="section-head__link" href="/videos/">All videos {{ icon("arrow") }}</a>
  </div>
  {%- for group in videoGroups %}
  {%- set list = videos | byGroup(group.key) | rejectattr("featured") %}
  <section class="video-group" aria-labelledby="home-{{ group.key }}">
    <div class="video-group__head">
      <h3 id="home-{{ group.key }}">{{ group.name }}</h3>
      <span class="hud-tag">{{ group.tag }}</span>
    </div>
    <ul class="vid-grid">
      {%- for v in list %}
      {%- if loop.index0 < 3 %}
      {% include "partials/video-card.njk" %}
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {%- if loop.index == 2 %}
  {%- set adSlot = "listing" %}
  {% include "partials/ad.njk" %}
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
  <p class="note">Videos are embedded from YouTube and belong to their creators. Nothing loads from YouTube until you press play. Links checked {{ site.videosChecked | readableDate }}.</p>
</div>

<section class="slang" aria-labelledby="slang-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="slang-heading">Speak the language</h2>
      <a class="section-head__link" href="/glossary/">Full glossary ({{ glossary.length }} terms) {{ icon("arrow") }}</a>
    </div>
    <ul class="term-grid">
      {%- for t in glossary %}
      {%- if t.term in ["Ace", "Clutch", "Entry frag", "Rocket jump", "Wallbang", "Frag movie"] %}
      <li class="term">
        <h3><a href="/glossary/#{{ t.term | slugify }}">{{ t.term }}</a></h3>
        <p>{{ t.def }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap">
  {%- if site.sale.enabled %}
  <section class="sale-callout" aria-labelledby="sale-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ icon("tag") }} Domain for sale</p>
      <h2 id="sale-heading">Respawn {{ site.domain }} as your brand</h2>
      <p>This domain is available. Five characters of pure gaming: ideal for a clan, esports team, highlights channel, tournament or FPS community. Send an enquiry and we will get back to you.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn--accent" href="{{ site.sale.path }}">Make an offer {{ icon("arrow") }}</a>
  </section>
  {%- endif %}

  <section class="faqs" id="faqs" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    {%- for faq in faqs %}
    <details class="faq"{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}>
      <summary>{{ faq.q }}</summary>
      <p>{{ faq.a }}</p>
    </details>
    {%- endfor %}
  </section>
</div>
<script type="application/ld+json">{{ videos | homeSchema({ "site": site, "title": title, "description": description, "faqs": faqs }) | jsonLd | safe }}</script>
